description:
Guests with no saved city and no GPS permission need a sensible default city instead of a hardcoded/broken one (P0-3 of the UX backlog). No such aggregate exists today (confirmed: grep for 'groupBy' in server/ shows no city-activity query; server/routes/fields.js:169-192 only has GET /cities, an alphabetical distinct list).

Add a new route directly after the existing `router.get('/cities', ...)` handler (server/routes/fields.js:169-192), before the '// Slim bbox query for map markers' comment at line 194:

```js
// Most active city by upcoming/recent game volume -- used as the guest default city
// (no saved city, no GPS permission) instead of a hardcoded literal.
router.get('/cities/top', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const rows = await prisma.$queryRaw`
      SELECT f.city AS city, COUNT(g.id)::int AS count
      FROM "Field" f
      JOIN "Game" g ON g."fieldId" = f.id
      WHERE f.city IS NOT NULL
        AND g.start >= NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days'
      GROUP BY f.city
      ORDER BY count DESC
      LIMIT 1
    `;
    res.json({ city: rows[0]?.city || null });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Get top city error:', error);
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Failed to get top city' });
  }
});
```

Follow the exact `prisma` import already used at the top of this file (do not re-import). This is a plain additive read-only route -- no schema/migration change, matches the Prisma-6/PostgreSQL stack described in server/CLAUDE.md. Response shape is intentionally `{ city: string | null }` (null when there are no games in the last 30 days at all) so callers can fall back to a static default without a second error branch.

Confirmed root cause of P0-2 (guest sport filter on /search has no effect on results/count/map): `gamesApi.search()` (next_app/src/services/api/games.ts:63-66) picks the backend endpoint by token presence:
```js
search: (params, token, signal) => {
    const endpoint = token ? '/api/games/search' : '/api/games/public';
    return apiClient<Game[]>(`${endpoint}?${params.toString()}`, { token, signal });
},
```
A guest's `getToken()` resolves to `null`/`undefined` (next_app/src/app/search/page.tsx:162,177: `const token = await getToken(); ... gamesApi.search(params, token || undefined, ...)`), so guests always hit `GET /api/games/public`. That route (server/routes/games.js:40-46 -> `getPublicGames`, server/services/gameService.js:1584-1608) destructures ONLY `{ fieldId, date, isOpenToJoin }` from the query -- `sport`, `q`, `city`, and the map bounding-box params are silently dropped, so sport selection, text search, city, and map-panning have zero effect for guests.

The fix is NOT a server change: `GET /api/games/search` (server/routes/games.js:113-119) already uses `attachOptionalUser` (not `authenticateToken`) -- confirmed in server/utils/auth.js:53-58, it calls `next()` immediately when there's no Authorization header, so `searchGames(req.query, undefined)` runs the full filter pipeline (server/services/gameService.js:986-1092, sport filter at lines 1037-1039) for guests exactly like for authenticated users; `buildVisibilityWhere(undefined)` (gameService.js:318-326) already correctly restricts guests to non-friends-only games only, same visibility `/public` provides today.

Fix: in `next_app/src/services/api/games.ts`, change the `search` method to always call `/api/games/search`, regardless of token:
```ts
search: (params: URLSearchParams, token?: string, signal?: AbortSignal) => {
    return apiClient<Game[]>(`/api/games/search?${params.toString()}`, { token, signal });
},
```
Do not remove the `/api/games/public` server route or `getPublicGames` service function in this task -- out of scope, no other caller currently depends on this change beyond what's listed here (confirmed via grep: the only web caller of `gamesApi.search` is `next_app/src/app/search/page.tsx:177` and `next_app/src/hooks/useGamesByDate.ts:60`, both benefit identically from this fix, no other file needs edits).

Per P0-5: all failures currently collapse into the single generic string "אירעה שגיאה בטעינת הנתונים" (`getLoadErrorMessage`, next_app/src/utils/apiError.ts:15-20), differentiating only 429. Retry already exists everywhere this is used (`InlineErrorRow.tsx` renders a "נסה שוב" button wired to `onRetry` in every consumer -- GamesByDateClient.tsx:154, GamesByCityClient.tsx:62-67, GamesByFriendsClient.tsx:42-47, MyJoinedGames.tsx:39-45, search/page.tsx:496-497) so no retry-wiring changes are needed, only the message differentiation.

Confirmed error shape available to differentiate on: `apiClient()` (next_app/src/services/api/client.ts:46-66) throws a plain `Error` with `.status` set to the HTTP status code for any non-2xx response (line 51-53); a genuine network/offline failure (fetch itself rejects, e.g. `TypeError: Failed to fetch`) reaches the same `catch` block and gets rethrown WITHOUT a `.status` property, so `getErrorStatus(error)` (apiError.ts:5-11) already reliably returns `undefined` for offline/network failures and a real HTTP status for server responses -- this mirrors the pattern already proven in `mapFriendRequestError` (apiError.ts:33-49, lines 44-45: `if (normalized.includes("failed to fetch") || normalized.includes("networkerror")) return "בעיית תקשורת, בדוק את החיבור לאינטרנט";`).

Rewrite `getLoadErrorMessage` (lines 15-20) to:
```ts
export function getLoadErrorMessage(error: unknown): string {
  const status = getErrorStatus(error);
  if (status === 429) return "יותר מדי בקשות, נסה שוב בעוד רגע";
  if (status === 401 || status === 403) return "יש להתחבר מחדש כדי לצפות בתוכן הזה";
  if (typeof status === "number" && status >= 500) return "שגיאת שרת זמנית, נסה שוב בעוד רגע";
  if (status === undefined) {
    const raw = error instanceof Error ? error.message.toLowerCase() : "";
    if (raw.includes("failed to fetch") || raw.includes("networkerror") || raw.includes("network request failed")) {
      return "בעיית תקשורת, בדוק את החיבור לאינטרנט ונסה שוב";
    }
  }
  return "אירעה שגיאה בטעינת הנתונים";
}
```
Apply the identical differentiation to `getActionErrorMessage` (lines 23-28), keeping its distinct base fallback string ("אירעה שגיאה, נסה שוב") for the final `return`. Do not change `mapFriendRequestError` (lines 33-49) -- it already has its own, more specific differentiation and is out of scope here. No changes needed in any consumer file -- `InlineErrorRow` and every call site already just render whatever string these functions return.

Per P1-8: confirmed `next_app/src/components/GamesByDateClient.tsx:119-129` renders the "רשת המכרים" toggle `Button` with no explanation, and confirmed server-side (`server/services/gameService.js:993`, `if (networkGames === 'true' && viewerId) { ... }`, no `else`) that for a guest (`viewerId` undefined) the toggle silently does nothing -- no error, no different results, no feedback that it had zero effect.

This file already imports `useUser` and has `const { user } = useUser();` (confirmed at line ~39 in the current file). Replace the `Button` at lines 120-128 with a `Tooltip`-wrapped version that also disables it for guests and shows an active-state indicator:
```tsx
<Tooltip title={user ? "מציג משחקים של חברים וחברים של חברים" : "זמין למשתמשים מחוברים בלבד"}>
  <span>
    <Button
      variant={networkGames ? "contained" : "outlined"}
      size="small"
      disabled={!user}
      onClick={() => setNetworkGames(!networkGames)}
      startIcon={<GroupIcon />}
      endIcon={networkGames ? <Chip size="small" label="פעיל" sx={{ height: 18, fontSize: "0.65rem", bgcolor: "rgba(255,255,255,0.25)", color: "inherit" }} /> : undefined}
      sx={{ borderRadius: 8, textTransform: "none", fontWeight: 600 }}
    >
      רשת המכרים
    </Button>
  </span>
</Tooltip>
```
(The `<span>` wrapper around a `disabled` `Button` is required for MUI `Tooltip` to still show on hover/focus -- a disabled native button element doesn't fire the pointer events `Tooltip` listens for otherwise.) Add imports: `import Tooltip from "@mui/material/Tooltip";`, `import Chip from "@mui/material/Chip";` (check `Chip` isn't already imported in this file first). Also add `setNetworkGames(false)` is NOT needed as a guest guard elsewhere -- `disabled` on the button already prevents a guest from ever setting `networkGames` to `true` via this control.
